    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 only one test class (`AcceptanceTest`) exists (the others are support classes), and `BUILD SUCCESS` with `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the customerCode collision de-duplication in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n- The `customerCode(Owner)` method still computes the base code `'<REGION>-<HASH8>'` as before.\n- It now collects the set of customer codes already assigned to existing owners. If the base code is free, it's returned unchanged. Otherwise it appends `'-<n>'`, incrementing `n` starting from `2` until it finds a code no existing owner holds, and returns that de-duplicated value.\n- Added the `java.util.stream.Collectors` import (`java.util.Set` was already present).\n\nThis satisfies the spec's guarantee that distinct owners always receive distinct customer codes, which is exactly what `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` asserts.",
